// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - MuseumUrn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3524833866" "Crate"
// Description :
"P4283356631" "Find the Xiong Hnub So"
// InteractBeginString :
"P2185545326" "You begin opening the crate."
// InteractInterruptedString :
"P535631865" "You have been interrupted."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1482095964" "You found an ancient urn tucked snugly inside the crate."
// InteractActionString :
"P1143515829" "Opening..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P822668034" "You found the urn that was intended for Graham's opening exhibit."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P483405818" "Enraged Tsoo"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P330673213" "You will suffer for this indignation!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P856364347" ""
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1127431811" "Hello, {HeroName}."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P355506204" "This... this will not be the end! No one may dishonor the Tsoo!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2868015113" "You recovered the Xiong Hnub So from the Tsoo."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3282798213" "<color orange>Graham claps excitedly when he looks inside the crate.</color><br><br>Oh, goodness, that's IT! That's the centerpiece to my exhibit! Oh, and it's barely marred at all!<br><br>I expected those ruffians to manhandle the urn, you see. Men like that have no real appreciation for fine art. I'm thankful they at least saw enough value in it to keep it safe.<br><br><color orange>Graham swoons over the urn for a while longer, then turns his attention back to you.</color><br><br>Oh! {HeroName}, you absolutely MUST come to the opening exhibit! If it weren't for you, I don't know what I would have done!"
// RandomFameString :
"P3882022333" "Hey, that's {HeroName}! I wonder why {Hero.gender=male his|her} face has been on all of those museum posters..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4000745720" "<color orange>Graham beams at you, making grandiose gestures at you as he talks.</color><br><br>I simply won't take no for an answer, {HeroName}! This will be the grand opening of what is soon to be the most prestigious art museum in the city, and it is all thanks to <b>you</b>! You <i>must</i> attend!<br><br>All of the most important and influential members of the local art community will be there, and I want to show you off to all of them. Oh, this will be <i>wonderful</i>!"
// AcceptString :
"P515651057" "If you insist..."
// SendOffString :
"P3331238838" "Oh, but I <i>do</i>, {HeroName}! You will be the guest of honor, as thanks for your efforts.<br><br><color orange>Graham loses a bit of his steam, and he looks down at his feet guiltily.</color><br><br>Plus, I may have already included you in some of the promotional materials I put together for the opening... but that's all fine now, because you're <b><i>coming</b></i>!<br><br><color orange>Graham seems to no longer be paying attention to you, lost in his own reverie.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4005270246" "Attend the Museum Opening"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4070561544" "Don't dawdle, we'll start the ceremony soon!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3580613246" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Guest of Dishonor</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3175682324" "You arrive at the time that Graham requested, to find that he's already begun his presentation.<br><br>At least that means you won't have to sit through the whole thing."
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3778701270" "Attend Graham's presentation"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3639772354" "Graham Easton"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3246054850" "The Tsoo again! They're after the urn - {HeroName}, do something!"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2275253406" "Hello there son"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P4114071661" "<t 5>...first time this exhibit has been shown in the United States. I'm very proud to-<t 3>Oh, here {Hero.gender=male he|she} is now.<t 3>Come on over, {HeroName}.<t 5>Ladies and gentlemen, I'd like to take a moment to address {HeroName}'s contribution to the exhibit.<t 4>Without {HeroName}'s intervention, the main exhibit of the show would be...<t 1><em none>What... what's happening?"
// Script Variable ACTOR1_NAME :
"P2095369878" "Museum Attendee"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3177773160" "Hello there."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1738482053" "Nevermind"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1128316674" "Tsoo Assassin"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3507094694" "Find {Hero.gender=male him|her}! {Hero.gender=male He|She}'s in here somewhere!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1692432827" "That's {HeroName}. Kill {Hero.gender=male him|her}!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P246784185" "The vengeance of the Tsoo can only be sated in blood!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3018526537" "Great honor to the one who brings me {HeroName}'s head!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3846096245" "Thunder Leopard"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYINFO :
"P641133420" "This Tsoo warrior uses strange techniques, the likes of which you haven't seen before. He appears to be able to channel electricity directly through his hands with each strike."
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1222872257" "{Hero.gender=male He|She} is capable in combat... as expected."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3850486086" "Your time is short, {HeroName}. You may stay my hand, but ten more will be waiting to strike you."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1058639849" "<d 6>Mark my words... we shall meet again. My master will not rest until you exist among the ancestors."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1876842306" "You fought off the Tsoo... but it didn't look like they were interested in the urn anymore."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2639439525" "<color orange>Graham pulls at his hair in frustration, making soft whimpering noises.</color><br><br>Aaaaaargh! Those brutes completely ruined the opening ceremony! If every exhibit goes this way, the museum will shut down in a <i>month</i>! This is insane!<br><br><color orange>Graham looks at you with pleading eyes.</color><br><br>Please, you MUST do something! I'm a taxpaying citizen, you know!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LedgerTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P3915270425" "<color orange>The Tsoo were clearly in a hurry when they cleared out of this warehouse, but you haven't come across any information that might help you learn who has put a price on your head.<br><br>You happen across a trash can, which appears to have been left unemptied. You don't know if it will hold anything useful, but it might be worth investigating..."
// Answer Text :
"P893781745" "(Empty the bin and examine its contents)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2545827813" "<color orange>No one ever told you that being a Hero would be glamorous...<br><br>You empty the contents of the trash can onto the floor, searching for anything that might contain useful information. A worn ledger catches your eye, and you pick it up.<br><br>Inside, it contains a detailed listing of the comings and goings of the warehouse. Illicit goods were brought here for storage until a buyer was found, then shipped off to various secondary locations.<br><br>You find the listing for the Xiong Hnub So, but it doesn't seem to have a listed buyer. Strangely, it doesn't even seem to be a part of the Tsoo's normal business prospects; it appears they never had any intention to sell the urn."
// Answer Text :
"P398922609" "(Try to find the name of the owner of the warehouse)"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P795300413" "<color orange>Near the front of the ledger, it lists a 'Master Sun Xiong' as both the owner of the warehouse and the manager of its affairs.<br><br>According to the ledger, Sun Xiong has far more holdings than this single warehouse, including a mansion located on the outskirts of Paragon City. It appears you have found a lead.<br><br>Just as you pocket the ledger and prepare to leave, you hear the sound of motion behind you!"
// Answer Text :
"P3534082821" "(Defend yourself!)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SunXiongTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P1869295831" "I am beaten and shamed in front of my own students. Finish me, and the contract on your life will end.<br><br><color orange>Sun Xiong looks up at you expectantly.</color><br><br>What are you waiting for, fool? Do not draw out my dishonor! Kill me!"
// Answer Text :
"P1673705252" "If that is your wish. [Kill Sun Xiong]"
// Answer Text :
"P3661017034" "I... cannot. Stand, warrior. [Spare Sun Xiong]"
// Page Kill Text :
"P2529360649" "<color orange>You deal Sun Xiong a swift, fatal blow. As Sun Xiong draws his final breath, the surrounding Tsoo do not seem like they will intervene.<br><br>It appears as though you have simply followed the Tsoo's philosophy: the strong prosper, and the weak perish."
// Page Spare Text :
"P3238234751" "<color orange>Sun Xiong glares at you, but struggles to his feet. He does not move for his weapon.<br><br>He stares at you for one long moment, as if unsure whether to be grateful or disgusted. Eventually, he bows to you slightly.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - GrahamTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P1286883155" "<color orange>Graham yelps as you approach. Even after recognizing you, he still appears to be wary.</color><br><br>{HeroName}! W-what do you want? Look, I appreciate what you've done for me, but...<br><br><color orange>Graham looks around nervously.</color><br><br>...but I really can't afford another Tsoo attack on my property. I'm sure you understand."
// Answer Text :
"P3967221988" "Excuse me? They only attacked me because of YOUR exhibit!"
// Answer Text :
"P50364738" "Graham... did you know that the Xiong Hnub So is tied to the Tsoo's ancestral line?"
// Answer Text :
"P2021191452" "*Sigh* Of course. Just wanted to inform you that the Tsoo won't be bothering you anymore."
// Page Indignant Text :
"P792283133" "<color orange>Graham cringes away from you, throwing up his hands defensively.</color><br><br>It's not my FAULT! I just wanted to open an art museum, and this... this unenlightened criminal excuse for a <i>city</i> keeps causing me no end of grief! I was just trying to add a little <i>culture</i> to this place!<br><br>Honestly, sometimes I wonder if it's even possible. Paragonians are just too... <i>brutish</i>."
// Answer Text :
"P232216040" "I can't believe I'm even hearing this. Goodbye, Graham."
// Page Curious Text :
"P2919710433" "<color orange>Graham's face pales, and he shrinks away from you.</color><br><br>N-n-now let's not jump to <i>conclusions</i>, I mean... one family shouldn't have a monopoly on fine art, you see. The public deserves a chance to...<br><br><color orange>As you continue to stare him down, Graham trails off.</color><br><br>Now look... I understand this may seem callous, but I have legal ownership of the piece. Whatever claims the Xiong family is making, they can't..."
// Answer Text :
"P72569167" "You're despicable, Graham. Don't call on me again."
// Answer Text :
"P1499068698" "I understand. Just... be careful what you show in your exhibits."
// Page Exasperated Text :
"P1238186453" "<color orange>Graham smiles weakly, and begins wringing his hands.</color><br><br>Oh... that's good news, I suppose. Yes, it is. Well, thank you, {HeroName}, for all of the trouble you've gone through.<br><br>Now, if you wouldn't mind leaving...?"
// Answer Text :
"P3323205114" "Nothing would make me happier, Graham. Goodbye."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2569830176" "The first order of business is to make sure that the urn is safe! I'm sure they're after it again, and I-"
// AcceptString :
"P1677357723" "Graham, I don't think they were after the urn."
// SendOffString :
"P880522271" "<color orange>Graham blinks at you, confused.</color><br><br>They weren't? But... why would they...<br><br>OF COURSE! They're after <i>YOU</i>! I should have <i>known</i> better than to invite a <i>Hero</i> to the opening ceremony of my exhibit. Well, I certainly hope you're planning on paying for the damages those hooligans caused in my museum! Why, the amount of work it will take to...<br><br><color orange>Graham is still ranting, but he doesn't seem to be saying anything worth your attention. You're fairly certain that the Tsoo are after you for some reason, and that it's connected to the urn somehow.<br><br>It might be a good idea to investigate the warehouse where they were originally storing the Xiong Hnub So, to get an idea of who has put a contract on your head.</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2337043278" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: More Important Things</color>"

